From 136ef0093d9f48481157a5a94bd924096115ee56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt-Xiaomi-RD16-port <rd16@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:04:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] qualcommbe: ipq53xx: add support for Xiaomi BE3600 (RD16)

Hardware: IPQ5332 (4x A53), 256 MiB RAM, 128 MiB W25N01KW SPI-NAND,
Motorcomm YT9215S switch (1x WAN + 3x LAN gigabit), 2.4 GHz IPQ5332 +
5 GHz QCN6432 Wi-Fi 7 (ath12k, hybrid AHB).

Installed into system slot A ("rootfs" MTD) only; slot B ("rootfs_1")
keeps the stock firmware and the stock U-Boot (bootmiwifi) falls back to
it after failed boots.

- DTS: NAND layout, switch, MACs from the U-Boot env, Wi-Fi (Q6 regions
  of the stock 256 MiB layout, memory mode 2, stock boot-args), reserved
  memory trimmed to what the stock DTB reserves;
- image: lzma FIT in UBI (kernel/rootfs/rootfs_data), factory.ubi and
  sysupgrade.bin; sysupgrade writes slot A and points U-Boot at it;
- base-files: U-Boot env, boot-OK flag reset, min_free_kbytes 8 MiB,
  no Q6 coredumps, Wi-Fi-less RAM-boot image, RPS + IRQ placement for
  the single EDMA RX ring, Wi-Fi defaults (RU, HE, 5 GHz ch 36,
  4 MiB mac80211 queue limit).
---
